Hi Denis,

I just committed a fix for the imageData(object)[,ix,iy] bug to Github and BioC devel.

If you have the devtools package and the R developer tools installed, you can install it with devtools::install_github("kuwisdelu/Cardinal").

Alternatively, you can install it from the developer version of Bioconductor once it's built (https://www.bioconductor.org/developers/how-to/useDevel/).

I don't have a built-in, user-accessible way to iterate through neighborhoods of pixels yet, but I will look into adding it for the next release.

-Kylie

